# Anti-aliasing switched in the pause menu (PERFORMANCE > ANTI ALIASING): msaa, fsr, off, fsr, msaa,
# the options and the temporal_aa mirror read after each. Run with a --toml that has stale
# temporal_aa and temporal_aa_available lines: they are ignored (transient) and stay as text.
wait 8s
mark title
press_until start left_title every=2s timeout=90s
mark map_zoom
wait_until roam 180s
mark settle
wait 3s
get mcla_anti_aliasing temporal_aa temporal_aa_available
press start 4f
wait 2s
press rb 4f
wait 1s
press rb 4f
wait 1s
press down 4f
wait 700ms
press down 4f
wait 700ms
press down 4f
wait 700ms
press down 4f
wait 700ms
press down 4f
wait 700ms
press a 4f
wait 1500ms
press down 4f
wait 600ms
press down 4f
wait 600ms
press down 4f
wait 600ms
press down 4f
wait 600ms
press down 4f
wait 600ms
press down 4f
wait 600ms
press down 4f
wait 600ms
press down 4f
wait 600ms
press down 4f
wait 600ms
press down 4f
wait 600ms
press down 4f
wait 600ms
press down 4f
wait 600ms
press down 4f
wait 600ms
press right 4f
wait 2500ms
get mcla_anti_aliasing temporal_aa temporal_aa_available
press right 4f
wait 2500ms
get mcla_anti_aliasing temporal_aa temporal_aa_available
press left 4f
wait 2500ms
get mcla_anti_aliasing temporal_aa temporal_aa_available
press left 4f
wait 2500ms
get mcla_anti_aliasing temporal_aa temporal_aa_available
press b 4f
wait 2s
mark end
wait 1s
